  endings:
  - id: end_no_air
    title: NO AIR
    body: The gauge hits zero. The recycler stops. The crew has been holding its
      breath for two days. The log records the last reading. The pen is still in
      the holder.
    priority: 100
    minSurvival: 0
    minScience: 0
    minMorale: 0
    maxSurvival: 0
    maxScience: 10
    maxMorale: 10
    requiredFlags: []
    forbiddenFlags: []
    requiredTags: 
    forbiddenTags: 
  - id: end_no_air_b
    title: THE LONG BREATH
    body: The last canister is logged, sealed and empty. The crew voted to stop opening
      the reserves. There is nothing to open. Someone winds the clock anyway. It
      is still ticking. It will outlast the air by a week.
    priority: 100
    minSurvival: 0
    minScience: 0
    minMorale: 0
    maxSurvival: 0
    maxScience: 10
    maxMorale: 10
    requiredFlags: []
    forbiddenFlags: []
    requiredTags: 
    forbiddenTags: 
  - id: end_no_signal
    title: NO SIGNAL
    body: The science station goes dark. The samples are still in the fridge. The
      fridge is still cold. Nobody knows how to run the fridge. The log has a line
      for this. The line is blank.
    priority: 100
    minSurvival: 0
    minScience: 0
    minMorale: 0
    maxSurvival: 10
    maxScience: 0
    maxMorale: 10
    requiredFlags: []
    forbiddenFlags: []
    requiredTags: 
    forbiddenTags: 
  - id: end_no_signal_b
    title: STATIC
    body: The telemetry breaks into noise on turn nine. Nobody can say what broke
      it. The crew keeps the screens on. The screens keep the lights on. The noise
      keeps the crew. Somebody swears there is a pattern in it. Somebody else starts
      to hear one.
    priority: 100
    minSurvival: 0
    minScience: 0
    minMorale: 0
    maxSurvival: 10
    maxScience: 0
    maxMorale: 10
    requiredFlags: []
    forbiddenFlags: []
    requiredTags: 
    forbiddenTags: 
  - id: end_no_voice
    title: NO VOICE
    body: The crew stops talking. The log stops being written. The ship runs. The
      lights are on. The seats are filled. Nobody is in them. The ship is doing fine.
      The ship is doing fine.
    priority: 100
    minSurvival: 0
    minScience: 0
    minMorale: 0
    maxSurvival: 10
    maxScience: 10
    maxMorale: 0
    requiredFlags: []
    forbiddenFlags: []
    requiredTags: 
    forbiddenTags: 
  - id: end_no_voice_b
    title: THE QUIET MESS
    body: Dinner is served on time. Six trays, six seats, no conversation. The chairs
      scrape, the trays clear, the lights dim. In the morning nobody remembers the
      meal. The roster does. The roster remembers everything now.
    priority: 100
    minSurvival: 0
    minScience: 0
    minMorale: 0
    maxSurvival: 10
    maxScience: 10
    maxMorale: 0
    requiredFlags: []
    forbiddenFlags: []
    requiredTags: 
    forbiddenTags: 
  - id: end_ark_sails
    title: THE ARK SAILS
    body: Everything holds. The air is sweet, the numbers are green, and the crew
      argues about movies instead of rations. The chart shows a coast that should
      not exist. The engines say you will reach it. For the first time, nobody on
      this ship is keeping a count of anything. There is nothing left to count against.
    priority: 90
    minSurvival: 9
    minScience: 9
    minMorale: 9
    maxSurvival: 10
    maxScience: 10
    maxMorale: 10
    requiredFlags: []
    forbiddenFlags: []
    requiredTags: 
    forbiddenTags: 
  - id: end_order
    title: ORDER
    body: The orders stand. The rounds are counted. The crew obeys without being
      asked. The log is full. The log is clean. The ship runs on time. Nobody remembers
      who wrote the first order. It does not matter. The order is the ship now.
    priority: 82
    minSurvival: 5
    minScience: 0
    minMorale: 0
    maxSurvival: 10
    maxScience: 10
    maxMorale: 10
    requiredFlags:
    - tamsin_oath
    - soldier_disarmed
    forbiddenFlags: []
    requiredTags: 
    forbiddenTags: 
  - id: end_reactor_priest
    title: THE REACTOR PRIEST
    body: The core is open. The shielding is gone. The engineer who opened it is
      still in the room. The room is warm. The ship is warm. The crew does not go
      near the room. The log says the reactor is fine. The log is written by the
      reactor now.
    priority: 78
    minSurvival: 2
    minScience: 6
    minMorale: 0
    maxSurvival: 10
    maxScience: 10
    maxMorale: 10
    requiredFlags:
    - reactor_open
    forbiddenFlags: []
    requiredTags: 
    forbiddenTags: 
  - id: end_mapped
    title: THE MAPPED COAST
    body: 'The map was right. Every badly drawn turn of it. The crew sails the route
      like a psalm, and the coast arrives exactly when the ink said it would. Whatever
      drew that map knew these waters. Nobody on board asks the only question that
      matters, which is: who is drawing the next one.'
    priority: 76
    minSurvival: 4
    minScience: 0
    minMorale: 0
    maxSurvival: 10
    maxScience: 10
    maxMorale: 10
    requiredFlags:
    - map_followed
    forbiddenFlags: []
    requiredTags: 
    forbiddenTags: 
  - id: end_greenhouse
    title: THE GREENHOUSE
    body: The dead soil grows. It took three failures and one near mutiny, but the
      racks are green and the smell is wrong in the best way. The crew eats something
      it grew. Nobody had eaten something that was alive an hour before. The ship
      is a farm now. Farms do not sink.
    priority: 70
    minSurvival: 6
    minScience: 4
    minMorale: 4
    maxSurvival: 10
    maxScience: 10
    maxMorale: 10
    requiredFlags:
    - seed_saved
    forbiddenFlags: []
    requiredTags: 08000000
    forbiddenTags: 
  - id: end_ward
    title: THE WARD
    body: 'The sick do not die. That is the whole miracle, and it takes all of it:
      the medic''s hours, the cold bunks, the rations nobody steals. The fevers break
      in order, like a list being worked. The last one up is the one who kept the
      list. She takes it down to the mess and pins it to the wall, finished.'
    priority: 68
    minSurvival: 2
    minScience: 4
    minMorale: 2
    maxSurvival: 10
    maxScience: 10
    maxMorale: 10
    requiredFlags: []
    forbiddenFlags: []
    requiredTags: 0500000007000000
    forbiddenTags: 
  - id: end_choir
    title: THE CHOIR
    body: It starts as humming in the ducts. Then the children carry it to the mess,
      and the soldiers stop pretending not to listen. By the fourth watch the whole
      crew is singing, badly, in three languages that agree on the chorus. The ship
      sails on the sound. It should not work. It works.
    priority: 68
    minSurvival: 2
    minScience: 0
    minMorale: 7
    maxSurvival: 10
    maxScience: 10
    maxMorale: 10
    requiredFlags: []
    forbiddenFlags: []
    requiredTags: 06000000
    forbiddenTags: 
  - id: end_new_crew
    title: THE NEW CREW
    body: The scan came back and nobody hid it again. The changed ones eat at the
      same table, work the same watches, and their names stay in the log without
      asterisks. Whatever the deep water is making, it signed the articles this time.
      The ship carries the first crew of two species, and the species gets along.
    priority: 70
    minSurvival: 3
    minScience: 3
    minMorale: 5
    maxSurvival: 10
    maxScience: 10
    maxMorale: 10
    requiredFlags:
    - mutant_kept
    forbiddenFlags: []
    requiredTags: 09000000
    forbiddenTags: 
  - id: end_engine_holds
    title: THE ENGINE HOLDS
    body: The engine was not built for this voyage, and it holds anyway. Every night
      it runs a little hotter, and every night the engineers swear a little quieter.
      It holds. The crew learns to sleep inside the noise. When it finally shakes,
      they hold the rail, and it holds.
    priority: 66
    minSurvival: 7
    minScience: 3
    minMorale: 0
    maxSurvival: 10
    maxScience: 10
    maxMorale: 10
    requiredFlags: []
    forbiddenFlags: []
    requiredTags: 00000000
    forbiddenTags: 
  - id: end_someone_small
    title: SOMEONE SMALL
    body: The future of the species is nine years old and currently grounded for
      stealing engine grease. She draws on the checklists, names the pumps, asks
      the questions that have no answers. The crew keeps her alive the way you keep
      a match alive. Something to carry across. Something to strike on the other
      side.
    priority: 66
    minSurvival: 4
    minScience: 4
    minMorale: 6
    maxSurvival: 10
    maxScience: 10
    maxMorale: 10
    requiredFlags: []
    forbiddenFlags: []
    requiredTags: 03000000
    forbiddenTags: 
  - id: end_lab
    title: THE LAB
    body: 'The lab hums through the last stretch. Everything the crew survived is
      written up, dated and filed: the fever, the mutation, the air. The conclusions
      will reach land before the stories do, and they will save more people than
      the ship ever carried. The crew is small. The data is not.'
    priority: 65
    minSurvival: 2
    minScience: 8
    minMorale: 2
    maxSurvival: 10
    maxScience: 10
    maxMorale: 10
    requiredFlags: []
    forbiddenFlags: []
    requiredTags: 
    forbiddenTags: 
  - id: end_clean_air
    title: CLEAN AIR
    body: The gauges settle at six and stay there. No alarms, no cannibalised parts,
      no speeches in the mess. The crew fixed what was broken and did not break anything
      that worked. It is the most boring voyage in the history of the service. The
      log says so. Nobody has ever been prouder of a boring log.
    priority: 62
    minSurvival: 6
    minScience: 6
    minMorale: 6
    maxSurvival: 8
    maxScience: 8
    maxMorale: 8
    requiredFlags: []
    forbiddenFlags: []
    requiredTags: 
    forbiddenTags: 
  - id: end_hold
    title: THE HOLD
    body: 'Nobody dies. That is the report, and the report is the achievement. The
      air is thin, the science is thin, the jokes are thin. The crew walks through
      the ship like tired men carrying furniture. The ark holds together, and the
      crew holds on. Some voyages are just this: not losing.'
    priority: 30
    minSurvival: 3
    minScience: 3
    minMorale: 3
    maxSurvival: 7
    maxScience: 9
    maxMorale: 7
    requiredFlags: []
    forbiddenFlags: []
    requiredTags: 
    forbiddenTags: 
  - id: end_drift
    title: DRIFT
    body: The ark does not sink and does not arrive. The current takes it somewhere
      the chart does not cover. The crew learns the sound of the hull and the smell
      of the recycled air, and then forgets there was ever another kind. The log
      keeps the count of days. The count is wrong. It does not matter.
    priority: 0
    minSurvival: 0
    minScience: 0
    minMorale: 0
    maxSurvival: 10
    maxScience: 10
    maxMorale: 10
    requiredFlags: []
    forbiddenFlags: []
    requiredTags: 
    forbiddenTags: 
  synergies:
  - id: syn_eng_sol
    tagA: 0
    tagB: 4
    countB: 1
    survival: 1
    science: 0
    morale: -1
    setFlag: 
    text: The engineer builds it. The soldier aims it.
  - id: syn_med_sick
    tagA: 5
    tagB: 7
    countB: 1
    survival: 1
    science: 0
    morale: 1
    setFlag: 
    text: She has one patient and no supplies. She improvises.
  - id: syn_eng_eng
    tagA: 0
    tagB: 0
    countB: 2
    survival: 1
    science: 1
    morale: -1
    setFlag: 
    text: Two engineers means one argument per bolt.
  - id: syn_child_dream
    tagA: 3
    tagB: 6
    countB: 1
    survival: 0
    science: 0
    morale: 2
    setFlag: 
    text: The child asks what the stars are called. Someone answers.
  - id: syn_sick_sick
    tagA: 7
    tagB: 7
    countB: 2
    survival: -1
    science: 0
    morale: -1
    setFlag: 
    text: They share a bunk. They share everything now.
  - id: syn_sol_mut
    tagA: 4
    tagB: 9
    countB: 1
    survival: 0
    science: 0
    morale: -2
    setFlag: 
    text: The soldier sleeps with the locker key on a string.
  - id: syn_farm_stub
    tagA: 8
    tagB: 1
    countB: 1
    survival: 1
    science: 0
    morale: 0
    setFlag: 
    text: The soil is bad. She plants anyway. The soil loses.
  - id: syn_sci_mut
    tagA: 2
    tagB: 9
    countB: 1
    survival: 0
    science: 1
    morale: -1
    setFlag: 
    text: The sample is labelled. The sample is also crew.
  - id: syn_med_med
    tagA: 5
    tagB: 5
    countB: 2
    survival: 1
    science: 0
    morale: 0
    setFlag: 
    text: One keeps the log. One keeps the hands steady.
  - id: syn_child_sick
    tagA: 3
    tagB: 7
    countB: 1
    survival: 0
    science: 0
    morale: -1
    setFlag: 
    text: The child is not allowed near that bunk. She goes anyway.
  - id: syn_stub_stub
    tagA: 1
    tagB: 1
    countB: 2
    survival: -1
    science: 0
    morale: 1
    setFlag: 
    text: Nobody backs down. Somehow the work still gets done.
  - id: syn_dream_sick
    tagA: 6
    tagB: 7
    countB: 1
    survival: 0
    science: -1
    morale: 1
    setFlag: 
    text: He describes the surface. Some of it is invented.
  - id: syn_eng_mut
    tagA: 0
    tagB: 9
    countB: 1
    survival: 0
    science: 1
    morale: -1
    setFlag: 
    text: The hands fit where the tools do not. Nobody records it.
  - id: syn_farm_farm
    tagA: 8
    tagB: 8
    countB: 2
    survival: 1
    science: 0
    morale: 1
    setFlag: 
    text: Two sets of rows. One harvest.
  - id: syn_sci_sci
    tagA: 2
    tagB: 2
    countB: 2
    survival: 0
    science: 2
    morale: -1
    setFlag: 
    text: The lab never sleeps. The results arrive at three and nobody signs them.
  - id: syn_farm_dream
    tagA: 8
    tagB: 6
    countB: 1
    survival: 1
    science: 0
    morale: 1
    setFlag: 
    text: He describes the fields they will plant on land. She starts the seeds tonight.
